  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Suppose $R$ is a $4\\times 5$ matrix and $S$ is a  $2\\times 4$ matrix. What are the dimensions of $SR?$",
  "worked_solution": "There are $4$ columns in $S$ and $4$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ equals the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $S$ and $R$ are conformable for multiplication, and $SR$ is a $2\\times 5$ matrix:\n\n$$\n{R}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{S}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 5}={SR}_{2\\times 5}\n$$",
